       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4,250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day for extended-release. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above any standard dose. This dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard tablet strength\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** two or three times daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If you really do intend 4,250 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away as oral, three times daily with meals."
