       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 12,750 mg/day it is about five times the maximum daily dose, and no indication supports it. Metformin doesn't work better above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day, and the main effect of going higher would be a greater risk of severe lactic acidosis. I'd be putting a patient at serious risk of harm if I entered it as written.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter up to 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) right now, or another dose you choose.\n- **Review with pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, a clinical pharmacist can review it with you. They can also enter it through the hospital's override process.\n- **Check for a different intent.** For example, you may have meant another drug or a different unit.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
